WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:23.400
. Let me ask you a question.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.050
What do you think is the real corona virus
death toll?

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:33.840
It appears it could be more than 54 thousand
deaths higher than the official death toll.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.550
And I'm going to explain how the CDC data
points us to that conclusion in a second.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:44.940
But at least to start, theoretically, anytime
you have something as big as a pandemic which

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.390
infects more than five million people in the
United States, where it 5.2 million official

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:55.480
cases to a country of more than 330 million
people, people die every day for corona virus

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.570
and other reasons.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:57.720
There are co morbidities.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.260
There are other factors.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:04.600
It's going to be unlikely that the official
death toll is exactly what the real death

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.530
toll is for the virus.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:11.820
Now, on the one side, there are conspiracy
theories from the right that are about deception

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:16.220
and politics, where they say the real death
toll is much lower.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:18.160
It's not 166 thousand.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.530
It's much smaller.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.030
They claim this is not me.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.050
This is the arguments some on the right make.

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:27.210
A lot of deaths are being counted as coronavirus
and they're really not.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:31.350
And they'll talk about someone died in a car
crash and a hospital counted.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:36.060
It is coronavirus because they get more money
that way or whatever, or Democrats are lying

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:41.119
and blowing up the death rate in order to
make political points or whatever the case

00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:42.119
may be.

00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:44.189
Now, you should be skeptical of that theory.

00:01:44.189 --> 00:01:49.440
And indeed, there's no evidence for that theory
other than if you want to be anecdotal.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.460
There might be cases where it's not a car
accident.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:57.840
But, you know, it's an infection caused by
a comorbidity in an elderly person who had

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:58.950
corona virus.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:04.090
And maybe there's like some debate as to should
this or shouldn't this count as a corona virus

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.090
death.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:10.469
But these are small numbers of situations
in a country with 5.2 million infections.

00:02:10.469 --> 00:02:13.029
You're bound to have some anecdotes like that.

00:02:13.029 --> 00:02:17.790
But on the other side, there's a much more
compelling reason to think the real corona

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:21.579
virus death toll is dramatically higher than
the official.

00:02:21.579 --> 00:02:24.209
And it is something called excess deaths.

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:32.739
The number of extra deaths during the March
to July period suggests that more than 54000

00:02:32.739 --> 00:02:39.889
additional people have died of coronavirus
be above and beyond the official death toll.

00:02:39.889 --> 00:02:44.939
This is derived when you look at excess deaths
and in the United States because we have so

00:02:44.939 --> 00:02:51.189
many people and so many years of data and
such detailed statistics about disease.

00:02:51.189 --> 00:02:56.890
We know how many people on average will die
of all causes based on our population, based

00:02:56.890 --> 00:02:59.260
on what's called the normal amount of death.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:04.409
We know, okay, if you add up expected car
accident deaths, cancer deaths, heart disease,

00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:10.620
flu altogether, we know when you don't have
a pandemic how many people typically die.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:16.109
And if you look at the deaths we would expect
from March 15th to July 25th.

00:03:16.109 --> 00:03:17.419
You see that during those dates.

00:03:17.419 --> 00:03:23.090
There were almost 200, 1000 excess deaths,
deaths beyond what we would normally have.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:28.720
And during that time, the official coronavirus
death toll was only 140, 7000.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:35.230
That leaves about 54000 extra deaths not officially
attributed to coronavirus.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:43.510
Now, epidemiologists favor looking at excess
deaths to gauge the impact of a pandemic because

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:49.129
excess deaths don't depend on testing people
and knowing exactly who had the virus.

00:03:49.129 --> 00:03:54.519
Posthumous testing, testing when someone goes
into the hospital, et cetera.

00:03:54.519 --> 00:04:00.080
And indeed, when you look at excess deaths,
everything tracks consistently with this theory.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:06.260
If you look at where the excess deaths disproportionately
are, it's in the states hardest hit by corona

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:07.260
virus.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:12.090
And it is a very coherent story that excess
death analysis points us do.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:19.430
So in all likelihood, the real coronavirus
death toll right now is at least 54000 deaths

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:20.930
higher than the original one.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:25.830
It's even more because that was March 15 to
July 25.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:30.740
In the two weeks since July 25, we've had
a resurgence in deaths and in all likelihood,

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.680
there are more uncounted deaths during that
period.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:37.360
So what is the likely real coronavirus death
toll?

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.689
Remember, official is 166.

00:04:39.689 --> 00:04:43.630
It's probably somewhere around 225 to 235.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:47.659
And rapidly approaching 250000 deaths.

00:04:47.659 --> 00:04:53.270
We are going to have to accept that the death
toll is much higher than many think.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:58.540
When the pandemic is so widespread, when tests
are still today taking five to seven days

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:04.000
or longer to come back with results, we know
we aren't capturing all the cases and therefore

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.530
it follows.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:08.229
We're not capturing all the deaths either.

00:05:08.229 --> 00:05:15.759
We later will have to see what is the long
term impact on the lungs, on the heart, on

00:05:15.759 --> 00:05:18.780
other systems from having and recovering from
corona virus.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:24.189
Because you could have a situation where years
down the line, there are premature deaths

00:05:24.189 --> 00:05:29.889
caused by damage done to vital organs by corona
virus.

00:05:29.889 --> 00:05:31.330
We don't know the extent of that yet.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:34.030
That's something the medical community is
looking at.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:35.719
Any deaths are tragic.

00:05:35.719 --> 00:05:40.050
We have many unnecessary deaths due to the
failed Trump response.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:44.530
But we also just have to face the reality
that by now we probably have somewhere between

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:51.719
55 and 60000 deaths that are not in the official
death count, which are due to corona virus,

00:05:51.719 --> 00:05:56.139
which gets us to what happens in November.

